{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "FDA",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case arose after the FDA\u2019s 2016 determination that e\u2011cigarettes are tobacco products, prompting retailers to seek review of an FDA denial order."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "scotus-23-1187",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "No court has ever held that an agency is \u201cadversely affected\u201d or \u201caggrieved\u201d under the APA."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Retailers are \u201cadversely affected\u201d by a denial order and are proper petitioners under \u00a7\u202f387l(a)(1)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Jackson (dissent) defined the \u201czone\u2011of\u2011interest test\u201d as a guide for deciding whether a plaintiff can challenge an agency decision."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissent), retailers have no procedural rights after a manufacturer submits its marketing application, and the FDA may deny an application without regard to retailer impact."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissent), congress may have intended to protect manufacturers\u2019 reliance interests without extending similar protection to retailers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissent), in the APA context, the zone\u2011of\u2011interest test is \u201cnot especially demanding.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissent), the majority fails to show how retailers are protected by \u00a7\u202f387j; they are not protected at all."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "45eca458b4c9706cb6cf62ef9761b3a544206ee8defe3927503f6c75364ab586",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-45eca458b4c9-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissent), retailers\u2019 participation was strategically important to circumvent venue restrictions, even though Congress did not intend to protect them."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Decision",
    "status": "complete",
